7. The presence of risk factors for QTc interval prolongation such as chronic hypokalaemia not corrected by complementary therapies, congenital or familial long QT interval syndrome, family history of unexplained sudden death in a first-degree relative under the age of 40 years, or initiation of Piratinib. Patients with a family history of unexplained sudden death in a first-degree relative younger than 40 years of age, or use of a drug that prolongs the QT interval and results in tip-twist ventricular tachycardia for ≤5 half-lives prior to the initiation of the first dose of ponatinib should be excluded.

   Patients with ≤5 half-lives of drugs that prolong the QT interval and cause tip-twist ventricular tachycardia prior to initiation of Brentinib should be excluded.
