12. patients being treated with warfarin or any other coumarin derivative anticoagulant, with the exception of low-dose warfarin (\< 2 mg) for the prevention of central catheter-related thrombosis;
13. presence of prior antineoplastic therapy toxicity not recovered to ≤ Grade 1 (NCI-CTCAE 5.0) or baseline, except for alopecia, skin hyperpigmentation, and Grade 2 peripheral neurotoxicity
14. any comorbid medical condition that may increase the risk of toxicity;
